tex-linebreak v0.9.0, MIT (package.json; the repository ships no LICENSE file), by Robert
Knight. Vendored files: dist/lib.js, dist/hyphens_en-us.js, each with its sourceMappingURL
line removed. Source: https://github.com/robertknight/tex-linebreak

lib.js implements the Knuth-Plass line-breaking algorithm ("Breaking paragraphs into
lines", Softw. Pract. Exp. 11(11), 1981) and carries a copy of hypher, the hyphenation
engine. hyphens_en-us.js holds the American English hyphenation patterns, which its own
header traces to the TeX hyphenation collection at tug.org. Both are UMD bundles: loaded
in a browser they leave texLineBreak_lib and texLineBreak_hyphens_en-us on the window,
which is how a deck uses them without a bundler.
